      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that calling `withoutAllowSetters()` on a `Value` that already has `allowSetters=false` returns the same instance (identity optimization), while preserving other settings (`ignoreUnknown=true`, `allowGetters=true`, `merge=false`).\n\nLet me write the improved version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version adds a descriptive method name (`test_withoutAllowSetters_isNoOpWhenAllowSettersAlreadyFalse`), a Javadoc comment explaining the scenario, named boolean arguments via inline comments, and assertion messages that clarify the intent — all without changing the runtime behaviour."
